# reDream server settings — one file for docker compose and local development.
#
#   sh scripts/init-env.sh     # copies this file to .env (mode 600) and fills
#                              # in POSTGRES_PASSWORD and INVITE_CODE
#
# Then fill in the LLM_* values below and run
#   docker compose up -d --build --wait
# Real values live only in the gitignored .env (NEVER commit them). Compose
# reads .env for its own ${...} values (compose.yaml) and hands every line to
# the server; environment variables set in compose.yaml win over this file.
# A value with a $ in it goes in single quotes, KEY='ab$cd': compose and
# uv run --env-file expand $cd otherwise (to nothing, if it is not set).

# ---- Required ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Chat LLM — any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint, one provider for
# every text role. Without these four, chat turns and the crisis check fail
# (the server still starts: GET /api/v1/health reports llm_ready false).
LLM_BASE_URL=
# Servers without auth (Ollama, vLLM without --api-key) still need a
# non-empty value, e.g. LLM_API_KEY=none
LLM_API_KEY=
# Replies, nightmare summary, summary extraction
LLM_MODEL=
# Routing, rewrite-safety segmenter + classifier, small checks
LLM_SMALL_MODEL=
#
# Mistral La Plateforme:
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# LLM_MODEL=mistral-large-2512
# LLM_SMALL_MODEL=mistral-small-2603
# LLM_SAFETY_MODEL=ministral-8b-2512
#
# Scaleway Generative APIs (a key restricted to a project other than the
# organization's default one needs https://api.scaleway.ai/<project_id>/v1):
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.scaleway.ai/v1
# LLM_MODEL=mistral-medium-3.5-128b
# LLM_SMALL_MODEL=mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct-2506

# Database password for the compose stack's Postgres (user and database
# "redream"); filled in by scripts/init-env.sh. Set it before the first
# docker compose up: the database volume keeps the first one. One you choose
# yourself: letters, digits and . _ ~ - only (it goes into DATABASE_URL as
# is; init-env.sh warns about anything else).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# The code people need to sign up while REGISTRATION_MODE=invite (the
# default); filled in by scripts/init-env.sh. 8 to 256 characters, or the
# server does not start. Share it with the people who may sign up.
INVITE_CODE=
# Only for the caddy profile: the domain Caddy gets an HTTPS certificate for,
# e.g. DOMAIN=dreams.example.org. Its DNS must point straight at this box
# (with Cloudflare: "DNS only", not proxied, or the rate limits see
# Cloudflare's addresses instead of the clients'), and ports 80 and 443 must
# be reachable. Switch the profile on here, so that every docker compose and
# make command (up, down, logs, update) includes Caddy:
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=caddy
DOMAIN=

# ---- Cost --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Accounts — the server's own email/password login.
# REGISTRATION_MODE: invite (default) = sign-up needs INVITE_CODE;
# open = anyone who reaches the server can sign up; closed = no sign-up in
# the app. Users can always be created (and passwords reset) with the CLI:
#   docker compose exec server python -m redream_api.cli create-user EMAIL
#   docker compose exec server python -m redream_api.cli set-password EMAIL
# and locally, from apps/server:
#   uv run --env-file ../../.env python -m redream_api.cli create-user EMAIL
REGISTRATION_MODE=invite
# Chat turns + transcriptions + rehearsal renderings per user per UTC day.
# Counted in memory: resets at UTC midnight and on restart. 0 = off. Set a
# spend limit at your provider too.
DAILY_AI_REQUESTS_PER_USER=100

# ---- Everything else (optional) ----------------------------------------------

# Database — plain Postgres 16+, async driver only (asyncpg; aiosqlite in
# tests). docker compose sets DATABASE_URL itself (its db service, with
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD) and ignores this line; it is for local development
# without compose. The server container applies migrations/ at start; locally,
# from apps/server, run
#   uv run --env-file ../../.env python -m redream_api.db.migrate   (or make db-migrate)
# The runner reads DATABASE_URL from the environment only (never this file
# directly; uv run --env-file or compose put it there), with the same
# ?options as the app (?ssl=require), and needs a direct or session-mode
# connection, not a transaction pooler.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres
# The host port of the compose server (bound to 127.0.0.1 only; default 8000).
# SERVER_PORT=8000
# The compose network's subnet (default 172.30.53.0/24); change it only if it
# clashes with a network the box already has. compose sets the server's
# FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS to it: X-Forwarded-For counts only from Caddy and the
# Docker proxy of the published port, and the rate limits see the client's
# address behind a proxy or tunnel that sets the header or appends to it.
# NETWORK_SUBNET=172.30.53.0/24

# Rehearsal audio — the MP3s are written under AUDIO_DIR (relative to the
# working directory; created on first write). It holds personal content:
# keep it on a persistent volume in a container (docker compose sets
# AUDIO_DIR=/app/data/audio on its audio volume), and know that it is deleted
# with the dream or the account. The server serves the files itself through
# links signed per process, so run exactly one worker.
AUDIO_DIR=data/audio
# Lifetime of a signed audio link, in seconds (60-3600, default 5 minutes);
# the app fetches a fresh one when it expires
REHEARSAL_URL_TTL_SECONDS=300

# Instance — shown in the app when people connect (GET /api/v1/instance).
# All optional; blank = not shown. Whoever runs this server for others is
# responsible for their data (the data controller): name yourself, say how to
# reach you, and link a privacy page.
# Up to 80 characters, e.g. INSTANCE_NAME="Dream Lab"
INSTANCE_NAME=
# Up to 120 characters: a person or an organisation
OPERATOR_NAME=
# Up to 200 characters: an email address or a URL
OPERATOR_CONTACT=
# Up to 500 characters: an absolute https:// URL (http:// only on localhost or
# 127.0.0.1, for local testing). Too long or another form, and the server
# does not start.
PRIVACY_URL=

# Chat LLM — tuning (the endpoint and models are under Required above).
# Crisis check (ADR 0005); empty = LLM_SMALL_MODEL
LLM_SAFETY_MODEL=
LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
# The crisis check blocks the chat turn, so it gets less
LLM_SAFETY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=20
# Ask for JSON output (response_format json_object); false for endpoints that
# reject it — the answers are then parsed out of prose or code fences
LLM_JSON_MODE=true
# Reasoning models get no temperature, max_completion_tokens instead of
# max_tokens, and LLM_REASONING_EFFORT. o1, o3, o4 and gpt-5 models are
# recognised by name; list any other here, comma-separated
LLM_REASONING_MODELS=
# low | medium | high (minimal: gpt-5 family only); empty = not sent, the
# provider's default. Mistral's reasoning models take only high (or none):
# with low they fall back to their default after one warning.
LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# Tokens added to a reasoning model's limit (max_completion_tokens) for its
# reasoning, which counts against that limit; 0 = none.
# A cap, not a charge: only the tokens the model generates are billed.
LLM_REASONING_EXTRA_TOKENS=2048
# A request the endpoint rejects (400 or 422) because it does not take
# temperature, top_p, max_tokens, max_completion_tokens, response_format or
# reasoning_effort for the model is sent again without it (max_tokens as
# max_completion_tokens and back); the endpoint and model keep that adjustment
# until restart and a warning is logged once.

# Rewrite-safety critic in the rewriting stage. false runs chat without it
# (a warning is logged at startup).
SAFETY_CRITIC_ENABLED=true

# Speech — optional, each half switched on by its model. Off: the route
# answers 503 {"detail": "voice_unavailable"} (after the consent check) and
# nothing is sent to a speech provider.
#
# Speech input (voice journaling): multipart POST {STT_BASE_URL}/audio/transcriptions
# with model, file (and language when known) — the OpenAI-compatible shape.
# Empty STT_BASE_URL / STT_API_KEY = LLM_BASE_URL / LLM_API_KEY. Set STT_API_KEY
# whenever STT_BASE_URL is on another host than LLM_BASE_URL: LLM_API_KEY is
# never sent to another host, so transcription stays off until you do (a
# warning is logged at startup). A server without auth
# still needs a non-empty value, e.g. STT_API_KEY=none.
STT_BASE_URL=
STT_API_KEY=
# Empty = transcription off
STT_MODEL=
#
# Speech output (rehearsal audio): POST {TTS_BASE_URL}/audio/speech.
# Empty TTS_BASE_URL / TTS_API_KEY = LLM_BASE_URL / LLM_API_KEY (same caveat as STT).
TTS_BASE_URL=
TTS_API_KEY=
# Empty = speech output off
TTS_MODEL=
# openai: {model, input, voice, response_format} -> the MP3 as the body
# mistral: {model, input, voice_id, response_format} -> base64 MP3 in "audio_data"
# Any other value stops the server at startup (chat included).
TTS_API_STYLE=openai
# Voice for every language; TTS_VOICE_EN / TTS_VOICE_DE override it per
# language. Speech output stays off while a language has no voice.
TTS_VOICE=
TTS_VOICE_EN=
TTS_VOICE_DE=
# A new model or voice renders a dream's audio anew on its next generation
# (the file name hashes model, voice, language and script).
#
# Mistral La Plateforme (pinned IDs, ADR 0010; Voxtral Transcribe 2 and
# Voxtral TTS 3; the German preset voice "Heidi" needs the TTS 3 model.
# Inputs are retained up to 30 days for abuse monitoring until ZDR is granted).
# The keys may stay empty only while LLM_BASE_URL is Mistral's too:
# STT_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# STT_API_KEY=
# STT_MODEL=voxtral-mini-2602
# TTS_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# TTS_API_KEY=
# TTS_MODEL=voxtral-mini-tts-3-0
# TTS_API_STYLE=mistral
# TTS_VOICE_EN=gb_jane_neutral
# TTS_VOICE_DE=voice_481
#
# Scaleway Generative APIs, STT only (no speech output there; zero-retention
# inference, ADR 0010's choice for raw voice). A key restricted to a project
# other than the organization's default one needs
# https://api.scaleway.ai/<project_id>/v1. The key may stay empty only while
# LLM_BASE_URL is Scaleway's too:
# STT_BASE_URL=https://api.scaleway.ai/v1
# STT_API_KEY=
# STT_MODEL=openai/whisper-large-v3:fp16
#
# OpenAI (gpt-4o-mini-tts is deprecated, shutdown announced for 2027-01-06;
# the voice names: alloy, ash, ballad, coral, echo, fable, nova, onyx, sage,
# shimmer, verse, marin, cedar). OpenAI takes at most 4096 characters of TTS
# input per request, and the whole rewritten dream goes in one: a longer one
# fails (502 on POST /dreams/{id}/rehearsal). The keys may stay empty only
# while LLM_BASE_URL is OpenAI's too:
# STT_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# STT_API_KEY=
# STT_MODEL=gpt-transcribe
# TTS_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# TTS_API_KEY=
# TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts
# TTS_API_STYLE=openai
# TTS_VOICE=marin

# Crisis pre-classifier
# DEV-ONLY: skip the crisis pre-classifier (ADR 0005). NEVER false in
# production — see the re-enable gate in docs/ROADMAP.md.
SAFETY_CLASSIFIER_ENABLED=true

# Helpline — what the app and the chat model point to when someone may need
# more than this exercise. Blank = a neutral default that names no country's
# numbers: the local emergency number and findahelpline.com.
# HELPLINE_TEXT_EN / HELPLINE_TEXT_DE: the full message shown in the app in
# place of the AI reply when the crisis check flags a message (German chats get
# _DE, every other chat _EN). At most 1000 characters, or the server does not start.
HELPLINE_TEXT_EN=
HELPLINE_TEXT_DE=
# HELPLINE_PROMPT_EN / HELPLINE_PROMPT_DE: a short reference inserted into the
# chat model's instructions; the model names it when a user is in real present
# distress. One line of at most 200 characters, or the server does not start.
HELPLINE_PROMPT_EN=
HELPLINE_PROMPT_DE=
# Put values with spaces in double quotes: without them `uv run --env-file`
# (make api-dev) warns and loads nothing from the file. The model gets the
# reference inside parentheses, so it should not contain any itself.
#
# Germany (TelefonSeelsorge):
# HELPLINE_TEXT_EN="It sounds like you might be going through something serious. This app is a self-help tool and can't provide crisis support. Please reach out to someone who can help right now: in Germany, the TelefonSeelsorge is available 24/7 at 0800 111 0 111 or 0800 111 0 222 (free and anonymous). If you are in immediate danger, call 112."
# HELPLINE_TEXT_DE="Es klingt, als würdest du gerade etwas Ernstes durchmachen. Diese App ist ein Selbsthilfe-Tool und kann keine Krisenhilfe leisten. Bitte wende dich an Menschen, die dir jetzt helfen können: Die TelefonSeelsorge ist rund um die Uhr erreichbar unter 0800 111 0 111 oder 0800 111 0 222 (kostenlos und anonym). In akuter Gefahr ruf bitte die 112 an."
# HELPLINE_PROMPT_EN="the German crisis line Telefonseelsorge at 0800 111 0 111, free and around the clock; in an emergency, 112"
# HELPLINE_PROMPT_DE="die Telefonseelsorge unter 0800 111 0 111, kostenlos und rund um die Uhr; im Notfall die 112"

# Runtime
ENVIRONMENT=development
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
